[{"name":"Pennylele/Almond-and-Chai-Blog","owner":"Pennylele","html_url":"https://github.com/Pennylele/Almond-and-Chai-Blog","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"MVC architecture, CRUD operations, user management system","topics":[],"score":246588,"global_rank":71107,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13851},{"name":"rachfop/shopping-cart","owner":"rachfop","html_url":"https://github.com/rachfop/shopping-cart","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":246582,"global_rank":71117,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13852},{"name":"mssrinivas/Distributed-File-Storage","owner":"mssrinivas","html_url":"https://github.com/mssrinivas/Distributed-File-Storage","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"This project provides a detailed explanation of the data replication part in the Distributed File Storage System. In a distributed system, data replication ensures reliability and availability among nodes: if one or more servers fail, the system can still function properly even though the node which contains the write is not available. The performance of the system can also be improved due to lower access time and higher scalability; we can reduce response time as the data can be acquired locally, and the system can scale better as requests can be serviced by multiple servers instead of one.","topics":[],"score":246582,"global_rank":71119,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13853},{"name":"DOH-SML1303/ncov_wa","owner":"DOH-SML1303","html_url":"https://github.com/DOH-SML1303/ncov_wa","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":246581,"global_rank":71124,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13854},{"name":"ChrisCalso/dog_breed_image_classifier","owner":"ChrisCalso","html_url":"https://github.com/ChrisCalso/dog_breed_image_classifier","stars":2,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"We used an image classifier to identify dog breeds. For this image classification task we used an image classification application using a deep learning model called a convolutional neural network (often abbreviated as CNN). CNNs work particularly well for detecting features in images like colors, textures, and edges; then using these features to identify objects in the images. I used a CNN that has already learned the features from a giant dataset of 1.2 million images called ImageNet. There are different types of CNNs that have different structures (architectures) that work better or worse depending on your criteria. With this project you'll explore the three different architectures (AlexNet, VGG, and ResNet).","topics":[],"score":246578,"global_rank":71126,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13855},{"name":"singfie/ConvexOptimizationMethods","owner":"singfie","html_url":"https://github.com/singfie/ConvexOptimizationMethods","stars":2,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A Collection of implemented methods for convex optimization in Python. These scripts were initially created to learn Convex Optimization methods and their implementation","topics":[],"score":246578,"global_rank":71127,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13856},{"name":"csosborn/roboat","owner":"csosborn","html_url":"https://github.com/csosborn/roboat","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":7,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":246575,"global_rank":71129,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13857},{"name":"Karthikram398/Smart_selfie","owner":"Karthikram398","html_url":"https://github.com/Karthikram398/Smart_selfie","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":246574,"global_rank":71134,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":13858},{"name":"rocket3989/ieeextreme14","owner":"